 "loinc": {
  "status": "NOT DONE",
  "reason": "LOINC is not hosted on EBI OLS4 (checked all 285 OLS4 ontologies). Its official FHIR terminology server fhir.loinc.org was initially blocked by the sandbox allowlist; network access was requested and GRANTED, after which every endpoint ($lookup, $expand, /metadata) returned HTTP 401 Unauthorized - the server requires a LOINC account, and no LOINC credential is configured. The NLM UMLS route (uts-ws.nlm.nih.gov) likewise returned 401 without a UMLS API key. No LOINC resolution rate is reported because none was measured.",
  "measured_rate": null,
  "to_enable": "add a LOINC (or UMLS/UTS) API credential, then re-run run_measure_eval.py with a loinc arm"
 },
 "recommendation": {
  "route_physiological_measure_to": "NCIT as primary, with SNOMED and CMO as declared fallbacks; KEEP HPO in the chain",
  "confidence": "moderate - measured on 387 of 2,944 unresolved unique names (13.1%)",
  "measured_basis": {
   "on the representative random 300": {
    "ncit": 0.0633,
    "snomed": 0.0367,
    "cmo": 0.0133,
    "hp": 0.01
   },
   "on the union of 387 names": {
    "ncit": 0.1214,
    "snomed": 0.0646,
    "cmo": 0.0413,
    "hp": 0.0103
   },
   "row_weighted_gain_if_all_three_added": "14.96% of the 5194 currently-unresolved physiological-measure rows"
  },
  "why": "NCIT beats HPO by ~6x on the representative sample (19/300 vs 3/300) and ~12x on the union, and the high-frequency stratum shows the gain concentrates where it matters: 33/100 of the most-repeated names resolve in NCIT vs 1/100 in HPO. CMO's names-resolved count is low but its hits are the highest-frequency cardiovascular measures (heart rate variability alone is 117 rows), so it earns inclusion on row weight, not name count. All three pass the decoy negative control at 0/14.",
  "caveats": [
   "Absolute rates stay low: even all three authorities together resolve only 14.2% of sampled names / ~15% of unresolved rows. Most physiological-measure names in this corpus are composite or instrument-specific ('orthostatic heart rate and blood pressure response', '19-item cdc long covid symptom list') and no terminology mints them. The majority will remain NULL, which is the correct outcome.",
   "NCIT's advantage is partly synonym-driven (13 of 47 union hits) and several NCIT synonym matches broaden the concept: 'cognitive function' -> 'PROMIS Cognitive Function Subordinate Domain', 'sleep quality' -> 'Sleep Quality Question', 'pulmonary function' -> 'Diagnostic Pulmonary Function Testing'. These are authority-asserted synonyms, so they are within discipline, but they map a measure onto an instrument item. RECOMMEND running NCIT exact-only for Tier 4 (34/387 = 8.8% of names, 465 rows) and holding synonym matches behind a review gate rather than admitting them silently.",
   "Multiple authorities per kind means one name can resolve differently in each. Route in a fixed declared order and record the minting ontology per the option-(b) provenance shape, so the tag stays truthful."
  ],
  "explicitly_not_recommended": "No authority is added for entity_kind 'other' or null. That kind has no coherent referent, so no authority is clearly right for it, and routing it anywhere would reintroduce the failure mode this architecture exists to remove. It stays unrouted."
 }
}